<% content_for :title, 'Terrestrial Planet' %>

<%= render 'help/page', title: 'Terrestrial Planet' do %>
  <div class='space-y-6'>
    <div class='space-y-3 text-fg'>
      <p>
        Displays the full survey record for a terrestrial planet. Data is organised into
        tabs corresponding to each digit of the Universal World Profile, plus supplementary
        tabs for orbital mechanics and the satellite inventory. Tabs for which no data has
        been recorded are still accessible but will appear empty.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class='font-semibold text-highlight mb-2'>Controls</p>
      <dl class='space-y-5'>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Regenerate</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Submits the body's Universal World Profile and orbital parameters to the
            generator data core, which recomputes and returns a complete characteristic
            profile. All existing survey data for the body is superseded by the returned
            values, including the satellite inventory — all previously recorded moons are
            expunged and reconstructed from the generator's output. This operation is
            irreversible. Available only when the body orbits a stellar primary.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div>
      <p class='font-semibold text-highlight mb-2'>Tabs</p>
      <dl class='space-y-5'>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Orbital</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Orbital radius (orbit number and/or AU), period, effective HZCO deviation,
            retrograde flag, inclination, eccentricity, tidal lock target, sidereal day,
            twilight zone status, and the location hierarchy through to sector. Jump shadow
            extent is shown when it exceeds the body's own shadow.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Starport</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Starport classification (A–E, X), allegiance, and travel zone. Berthing and fuel costs
            (WBH p. 257) are shown on the Starport tab and Planetary Profile, with a dash where a
            cost doesn't apply.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Physical</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Diameter (km), mass (Earth masses), surface gravity (g), density (Earth
            relative), mean temperature (°C), rotation period (hours), axial tilt,
            albedo, and greenhouse factor.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Atmo</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Atmosphere code and composition type. Tainted atmospheres include irritant
            subtype, severity, and persistence ratings. Hazard code is shown where applicable.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Hydro</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Hydrographics code, liquid type, and surface distribution pattern.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Pop</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Population code with approximate headcount range, concentration rating,
            urbanisation percentage, major city count, and cultural indices
            (cohesion, diversity, militancy, and related ratings).
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Gov</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Government type code and description, authority style, centralisation,
            and the structure of judicial, executive, and legislative bodies.
            Not shown when population and this value are both 0.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Law</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Law level code with sub-ratings covering weapons and armour restrictions,
            criminal and economic law, personal rights, uniformity, and judicial system.
            Not shown when population and this value are both 0.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Tech</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Overall technology level code with per-category ratings for electronics,
            energy, manufacturing, medical, environmental, land, sea, air, and space
            transport, and personal and heavy military equipment.
            Not shown when population and this value are both 0.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Moons</dt>
          <dd class='mt-1 text-fg'>
            Paginated list of satellites. The tab counter shows the total moon count.
            Toggle <span class='font-semibold text-fg-bright'>Significant only</span>
            to suppress sub-kilometre bodies.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class='pt-2 text-right uppercase font-mono text-xs tracking-[0.22em] text-fg-muted'>
      REFERENCE 0626TP
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>